Helm is k8s package manager it is like yum,apt,brew
yaml files stored in Helm

Key components of helm

1. Helm Client: it is basically a CLI tool to interact with k8s
2. Helm chart: Basically it is collection of manifest/yaml files
3. Helm Repo: it is location where helm charts are stored
4. Helm realease: realse version after charts apply to k8 cluster
	chart version
	app version
	
Benefits of Helm:

Simplifies deployment: Reduces manual YAML work
Version control: Helm maintain the version of application we can rollback to old version
Configuration Management: helm uses values files to manage the config of charts and we can customised according to our need
Reusable and Shareable : we can download charts and create our own if needed

Folder structure of helm charts

mychart/

│
├── Chart.yaml- 
├── values.yaml
├── charts/
├── templates/
│   ├── deployment.yaml
│   ├── service.yaml
│   ├── ingress.yaml
│   ├── configmap.yaml
│   └── _helpers.tpl
│
└── .helmignore

File/Folder	Purpose
Chart.yaml		Chart metadata
values.yaml		Configurations
templates/		Kubernetes manifests
charts/			Dependencies
_helpers.tpl	Reusable helpers(use to change common inputs)
				
				App name
				Labels
				Full names
				Common annotations
				Image names
				Chart names
				
